    "bio": "(served under the name of McMorris, Cathy in the One Hundred Ninth Congress and the name McMorris Rodgers, Cathy in the One Hundred Tenth through One Hundred Fifteenth Congresses), a Representative from Washington; born in Salem, Marion County, Oreg., May 22, 1969; graduated from Columbia River Christian Academy, Kettle Falls, Wash., 1986; B.A., Pensacola Christian College, Pensacola, Fla., 1990; M.B.A., University of Washington, Seattle, Wash., 2002; family orchard business; member of the Washington state house of representatives, 1994-2004, minority leader, 2002-2003; elected as a Republican to the One Hundred Ninth and to the nine succeeding Congresses (January 3, 2005-January 3, 2025); was not a candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Nineteenth Congress in 2024; chair, House Republican Conference (One Hundred Thirteenth through One Hundred Fifteenth Congresses); chair, Committee on Energy and Commerce (One Hundred Eighteenth Congress).",
